{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/925455-more-pathway-questions","id":925455,"title":"More pathway questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-03T12:24:08-07:00","id":925455,"title":"More pathway questions","content":"If you open a primordial pathway, it explains what happens when people in the merged location leave. They get sent to another chamber. What happens if someone enters the location after the merge takes place? Do they enter the scene? is the merged location gone from their perspective? And if they do enter the merged location, can they see it before walking in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T12:40:43-07:00","id":925465,"title":"","content":"Well if you look at the definition, the two areas are merged, so they are as one. I imagine if they enter while merged it would be the same as if they were present when the merge first happened, it's trying to leave that gets complicated. Unless they have some kind of dimensional sense (ala mage) then I doubt they could see anything unless there are traits that would be obvious (like fog in a building or something).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T13:02:54-07:00","id":925472,"title":"","content":"Say it's a chamber that exists in a graveyard, and youre able to call it down in an office, would both locations overlap, like gravestones in the office? Wouldn't people see such an overlap even without traits being in effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T16:50:31-07:00","id":925560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/925455-more-pathway-questions?p=925472#post925472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say it's a chamber that exists in a graveyard, and youre able to call it down in an office</div> </div> </div> </div>Important question: <i>How?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:10:50-07:00","id":925570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/925455-more-pathway-questions?p=925560#post925560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Important question: <i>How?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>By rolling wits+resolve -3 for material world +however many traits you're able to have up.<br /> <br /> Page 97 of rulebook","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1377,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","user":"Wrequis","date":". 07-03-2016, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:14:20-07:00","id":925572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/925455-more-pathway-questions?p=925570#post925570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By rolling wits+resolve -3 for material world +however many traits you're able to have up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Allow me to rephrase:<br /> <br /> Look at &quot;Chambers and Lair Traits&quot; on p101-2. What's the penalty for a level of similarity <i>below</i> descriptive similarity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:19:24-07:00","id":925575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/925455-more-pathway-questions?p=925572#post925572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allow me to rephrase:<br /> <br /> Look at &amp;quot;Chambers and Lair Traits&amp;quot; on p101-2. What's the penalty for a level of similarity <i>below</i> descriptive similarity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's only for applying lair traits in an area with no other lair traits, if you haven't or can't find a means to make one, to then call others.<br /> <br /> &quot; To impose Traits into a substitute location like this, the player must succeed on a Wits + Resolve roll, with a dice penalty based on how dissimilar the location used is.&quot;<br /> <br /> -page 101","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:32:33-07:00","id":925581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/925455-more-pathway-questions?p=925575#post925575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah that's only for applying lair traits in an area with no other lair traits</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Look again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p97</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts can\u2019t simply open Pathways between any realms they choose. As with many aspects of their Lair, it\u2019s the resonance, or similarity, between the Lair and somewhere else that affords access. <b>Opening a Pathway to the exact location from which the Beast created a Chamber is easiest, but desperate Beasts and cunning would-be intruders can use similar locations by incurring an additional dice penalty based on how well the location matches.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p101</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>As with opening a Primordial Pathway,</b> Beasts may attempt to use a Chamber in locations that are similar, if not exactly the same, by spending a Willpower point. To impose Traits into a substitute location like this, the player must succeed on a Wits + Resolve roll, with a dice penalty based on how dissimilar the location used is.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Using the exact location for a Chamber does not incur a dice penalty to <b>opening a Primordial Pathway</b> or imposing Lair Traits.<br /> [the running example specifically concerns attempts to open a Primordial Pathway being penalized by similarity]</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:41:11-07:00","id":925585,"title":"","content":"Hmm yeah I spent the last ten minutes reading it over and over, it's kind of tediously placed as it's not referenced on the chart on page 92, or in the back of the book for the easy access charts, very easily missed if not extremely scrutinised.<br /> <br /> Okay so back to my question, and I'll change it up to be more correct. if this beast is hunting someone in a mall, when one of their chambers is In another mall, and they get enough similarity and succeed on their roll to bring down their lair, would the geography change to kind of be both malls, so you'd be able to see statues posters or landmarks from both locations?<br /> <br /> And if so, could people looking in see it as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:46:09-07:00","id":925589,"title":"","content":"No Wrequis your mixing how the connection plays up. Opening the pathway doesn't connect the current location to where the chamber was originally made it connects the current location to the chamber. Think less portal gun and more Silent Hill's Otherworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:53:09-07:00","id":925591,"title":"","content":"I know they wouldn't be co located to the mall in which your chamber was made, but the chamber would be identical to the mall.<br /> <br /> So either A) the location would like like a combination of where you took them from, and what your chamber looks like<br /> B) it would look exactly like 'where you made the chamber from<br /> Or C) it looks like exactly where you opened the pathway, except now you're merged with your horror<br /> <br /> (Please inform me if I'm incorrect or which is the correct way)<br /> <br /> Either way if it's like silent hill then I feel like people entering scene after you opened the oathway would be oblivious to the people that are in the open pathway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T18:01:02-07:00","id":925598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/925455-more-pathway-questions?p=925591#post925591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know they wouldn't be co located to the mall in which your chamber was made, but the chamber would be identical to the mall.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're conflating the Chamber with its seed. The Chamber is a part of a shifting nightmarish realm of human terror and need not adhere to strict detailed correlation to the physical location that gave rise to it. Exact similarity is so potent because it replicates the circumstances that formed the Chamber, not because the Chamber is a precise copy of the seed location.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Either way if it's like silent hill then I feel like people entering scene after you opened the oathway would be oblivious to the people that are in the open pathway </div> </div> </div>The Pathway is typically open for less than a minute regardless, but the area's co-location with part of the Primordial Dream isn't itself a subjective quality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T18:24:13-07:00","id":925612,"title":"","content":"I mean you can roll an exceptional success and have it open for the scene, which is why I was curious about other passerbys.<br /> <br /> And yes I was definitely perceiving it to be exactly the same as the location vs it being a nightmare version of it, thank you for clearing that up, so the mall where you open the primordial pathway would just become a nightmarish version of itself and have any or all of your traits active.<br /> <br /> So if you've been in your lair for a while, you once again merge with an external area that symbolically relates to the chamber, and catch anyone accidentally standing around inside?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T19:27:19-07:00","id":925635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/925455-more-pathway-questions?p=925612#post925612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes I was definitely perceiving it to be exactly the same as the location vs it being a nightmare version of it, thank you for clearing that up, so the mall where you open the primordial pathway would just become a nightmarish version of itself and have any or all of your traits active.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mall where you open the Primordial Pathway would become entangled with the nightmarish mall that is part of your Horror's hunting grounds, which could look mostly the same as the external mall or be dramatically different, depending on the particulars of your Legend and your state of mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if you've been in your lair for a while, you once again merge with an external area that symbolically relates to the chamber, and catch anyone accidentally standing around inside? </div> </div> </div>Yup, though it's not for nothing that most Lair Traits coincide with locations people tend to avoid lingering in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T19:39:54-07:00","id":925640,"title":"","content":"Yeah but not only traits it has to be symbolic to the chamber itself, could pose a bit of a challenge just getting out of the lair lol.<br /> <br /> Thank you all for taking the time to help me get a better understanding of how this all works <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T00:27:42-07:00","id":925777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/925455-more-pathway-questions?p=925581#post925581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Look again.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking at this and it makes no sense. Why would info about opening pathways be sequestered in a section far removed from the one set aside for teaching you how primordial pathways work? There's no indication that this info would be located under lair traits. Did someone screw up in layout?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T11:01:05-07:00","id":925981,"title":"","content":"Most likely","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}